}
{\plain {\f0 \b0 In DSP, models that employ}{\ulnone 
\f0 \i0 \b  }{\ulnone \f0 \i0 \b random 
sequences}{\ulnone \f0 \b0  }{\f0 \b0  are
 of great utility. We want to enrich our
 models to be able to include degrading 
random effects such as noise. Mathematical
 and scientific applications are generally
 capable of generating at least a random
 variable uniformly distributed over (0,1)
 with repeated calls yielding a sequence
 of approximately independent random variables.
 Mathcad's}{\b \f0  }{\b0 \f0 built-in function}{\f0 
\b  rnd(a)}{\f0 \b0  generates a sample 
of a random variable uniformly distributed
 over (0,a). With suitable transformations,
 we can then generate more complicated random
 models. }}
}
