{\plain {We must often }{consider a sequence
 for indices outside the range for which
 it has been defined. For example, the translation
 of a sequence may be of interest. There
 are two natural and useful ways to extend
 the definition of a sequence to a greater
 range of indices: by zero padding and by
 periodic extension. We will illustrate 
the former method now and discuss the latter
 method in the next section. }}
}
