{\plain {\f0 This is an example of the }{\b 
\i0 \f0 zero padding}{\f0  operation. Often,
 but not always, the zeros are appended 
to the beginning or end of the sequence.
  }{\b \f0 \f0 ‡ }}
}
.TXT 9 0 211 0
Cg a50.000000,50.125000,589
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Times New Roman;}
{\f2\fnil Symbol;}
{\f3\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {In Example 1.6, we gave two ways
 to implement the zero padding operation.
 The first method used Mathcad's }{\b conditional
 if function}{ to explicitly implement the
 definition. }{We explicitly ask for s}{\fs16 
\dn6 n}{ only for n for which it is defined.}{
 The second method used the }{\b Boolean
 operator <}{ in }{the }{\b Boolean expression
 (n<M)}{ which takes on the value 1 when
 the }{condit}{ion is true and the value
 0 when the }{condit}{ion is false. }{We
 implicitly ask for s}{\fs16 \dn6 n}{ only
 for n for which it is defined. We will 
make frequent use of these functions.}}
}
