{\plain {Whereas }{\b READ}{ and }{\b WRITE}{
 are useful for data in vector form, }{\b 
READPRN}{ and }{\b WRITEPRN}{ are useful
 for data in matrix form. The }{\b structured
 file}{ time_alt.prn is data }{recorded}{
 from a rocket launch. It is comprised of
 26  (time,altitude) pairs. When read with
 READPRN, a 26 by 2 matrix results, with
 the first column being the set of times
 and the second column being the corresponding
 measured altitudes. Read the file, extract
 the columns as time and altitiude vectors
 and plot the altitude versus time. }{\b 
 }{\b \f0 ‡ }}
}
