}
.TXT 4 11 117 0
Cg a48.625000,50.000000,747
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Times New Roman;}
{\f2\fnil Symbol;}
{\f3\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {\i0 "Advanced}{\i  }{\i0 operations
 on digital sequences" is the heart of }{\i0 
\ulnone digital signal processing. Our interest
 here centers on }{\b0 \i0 \ulnone digital
 filtering}{\i0 \ulnone  of discrete-time
 signals, which  will be defined as}{\b 
\i0 \ulnone  }{\b0 \i0 \ulnone linear, invariant
 operations}{\i0 \ulnone  on sequences. 
Both the understanding and the efficient
 implementation of filtering- and other 
operations associated with digital signals-
  can be greatly facilitated using the}{\i0 
\b \ulnone  }{\b0 \i0 \ulnone Discrete Fourier
 Transform, DFT}{\i0 \b \ulnone ,}{\i0 \ulnone 
 implemented by a fast algorithm called 
the}{\b \i0 \ulnone  }{\b0 \i0 \ulnone Fast
 Fourier Transform, FFT}{\b \i0 \ulnone 
.}{\i0 \ulnone  We turn next, in order, 
to these subjects.}}
}
