{\plain {\f0 \b0 \i0 (a) Create a new Mathcad
 document and d}{\f0 \i0 \b0 \b0 efine an
 analog pulse train, a periodic repetition
 of a basic pulse. Use a function definition
 to implement the basic pulse and use Mathcad's
 ability to sum functions to implement the
 pulse train. (You will have to choose workable
 parameters.) Plot the analog signal.}}
}
.TXT 11 0 328 0
Cg a50.625000,50.250000,423
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Times New Roman;}
{\f2\fnil Symbol;}
{\f3\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {\f0 \i0 \b0 \b0 (b) Now }{\f0 \b0 
\i0 \f0 choose, independently for each pulse,
 an amplitude to be randomly +1 or -1. Such
 an amplitude sequence represents the encoding
 of a}{\b0 \f0 \i0 \i0 \f0  sequence of 
}{\f0 \b0 \i0 \f0 \b0 \i0 \f0  }{\f0 \b0 
\i0 \b0 \f0 \i0 \i0 \f0 binary}{\f0 \b0 
\i0  symbols into a (sampled) waveform that
 can be transmitted through a communication
 channel. Plot this communication signal.}}
}
.TXT 11 0 173 0
Cg a47.000000,50.125000,216
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Times New Roman;}
{\f2\fnil Symbol;}
{\f3\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {\f0 \b0 \i0 \f0 \b0 \i0 (c) The
 communication channel will a}{\f0 \b0 \i0 
\f0 \b0 \i0 \f0 \b0 \i0 dd thermal noise
 to the communication signal. It will be
 easiest to add this feature to our model
 a little later.}}
}
.TXT 7 0 329 0
Cg a49.625000,50.000000,178
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
